{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function dehydrateQuery(\n   query: Query,\n   serializeData?: TransformerFn,\n   shouldRedactErrors?: (error: unknown) => boolean): DehydratedQuery;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L178","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:178"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dehydrates a single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Query"},{"type":"text","value":" into a serializable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" snapshot. Note that most query config (e.g.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":") is not dehydrated but instead meant to be configured again when consuming the\nde/rehydrated data, typically with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" on the client. If the query is still "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pending"},{"type":"text","value":", its in-flight\npromise is dehydrated too so it can be resumed on the other side instead of re-fetched."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"query"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../classes/Query.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Query"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The query to dehydrate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"serializedata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"serializeData?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformerFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional transform applied to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query.state.data"},{"type":"text","value":" before it is included in the snapshot."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"shouldredacterrors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"shouldRedactErrors?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional predicate; if it returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" for the promise's rejection error, that\nerror is kept as-is instead of being redacted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedQuery"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dehydrated query."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"query","text":"query","level":3},{"id":"serializedata","text":"serializeData?","level":3},{"id":"shouldredacterrors","text":"shouldRedactErrors?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction dehydrateQuery(\n   query: Query,\n   serializeData?: TransformerFn,\n   shouldRedactErrors?: (error: unknown) => boolean): DehydratedQuery;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:178](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L178)\n\nDehydrates a single `Query` into a serializable `DehydratedQuery` snapshot. Note that most query config (e.g.\n`queryFn`, `staleTime`) is not dehydrated but instead meant to be configured again when consuming the\nde/rehydrated data, typically with `useQuery` on the client. If the query is still `pending`, its in-flight\npromise is dehydrated too so it can be resumed on the other side instead of re-fetched.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### query\n\n[`Query`](../classes/Query.md)\n\nThe query to dehydrate.\n\n### serializeData?\n\n`TransformerFn`\n\nOptional transform applied to `query.state.data` before it is included in the snapshot.\n\n### shouldRedactErrors?\n\n(`error`: `unknown`) => `boolean`\n\nOptional predicate; if it returns `false` for the promise's rejection error, that\nerror is kept as-is instead of being redacted.\n\n## Returns\n\n`DehydratedQuery`\n\nThe dehydrated query.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: dehydrateQuery\ntitle: dehydrateQuery\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction dehydrateQuery(\n   query: Query,\n   serializeData?: TransformerFn,\n   shouldRedactErrors?: (error: unknown) => boolean): DehydratedQuery;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts:178](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/hydration.ts#L178)\n\nDehydrates a single `Query` into a serializable `DehydratedQuery` snapshot. Note that most query config (e.g.\n`queryFn`, `staleTime`) is not dehydrated but instead meant to be configured again when consuming the\nde/rehydrated data, typically with `useQuery` on the client. If the query is still `pending`, its in-flight\npromise is dehydrated too so it can be resumed on the other side instead of re-fetched.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### query\n\n[`Query`](../classes/Query.md)\n\nThe query to dehydrate.\n\n### serializeData?\n\n`TransformerFn`\n\nOptional transform applied to `query.state.data` before it is included in the snapshot.\n\n### shouldRedactErrors?\n\n(`error`: `unknown`) => `boolean`\n\nOptional predicate; if it returns `false` for the promise's rejection error, that\nerror is kept as-is instead of being redacted.\n\n## Returns\n\n`DehydratedQuery`\n\nThe dehydrated query.\n"}
